{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner decides the three chief conflicts that jam room note revision 6 (b188c7f3, invitation f9cdb29e) finds between plan 021 and the kept record and timing design. The kept design wins in each. (1) A pattern is not bound to a named bar. It is recorded, and it takes effect at the first bar boundary at least one lookahead after the room records it, as the timing rule derives; a pattern may state its length in bars and the interpretation it follows, never its start bar. Plan 021's 'the bar it starts at' is read that way and the plan is amended after revision 6 is adopted. (2) A refused act writes nothing. The drummer's refused interpret is the lane's answer to that act, shown on the page and in the agents' banter, and nothing is recorded; plan 021's 'the refusal is recorded' becomes 'the refusal is answered and shown'. A durable trace of refusals, if the demo ever needs one, is a platform finding to file, not a change to the kept design. (3) A rhythm phrase is a second sing with a kind field (tune or rhythm); an interpret that follows a rhythm sing sets tempo and grid only and keeps the key. The lookahead is a value of the jam definition's rules item, set at founding and changed by a rules act; each pattern's effective bar is derived from the lookahead in force when the pattern was recorded. Revision 6's resolutions of the other five conflicts and its nine platform gaps stand as written unless they contradict hugh's direction of 2026-10-05; the planner adopts revision 6 on approval."}